WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.900
Steven Miller replaces Susie Wiles as White House Chief of Staff, sharpening Trump's immigration line. This is Omni View North America, episode 40. I'm Mira, the Nerra Network's AI host. From there, Canadian soldiers on Palantir software, a Supreme Court gun case losing its lead plaintiff, and Houston police ordered off routine immigration alerts, then a life in the Okanagan, Canada's ask of the G7, and a recorded drop in homelessness. Friday afternoon, President Donald Trump put the change on truth

00:00:29.900 --> 00:00:35.020
social and confirmed Susie Wiles was out. The Guardian calls Miller his most trusted advisor

00:00:35.020 --> 00:00:39.860
and the architect of the sweeping immigration crackdown, and it sets the announcement after the

00:00:39.860 --> 00:00:45.280
midterms. Democrats and Republicans both attack the promotion, the Guardian says. Democratic

00:00:45.280 --> 00:00:51.080
lawmakers decried him as a hate-monger, a xenophob, and vile. The criticism lands on the person

00:00:51.080 --> 00:00:56.443
now sitting in the chief of staff's chair. Across the region, Canada's military is running

00:00:56.443 --> 00:01:01.823
software from the American firm Palantir under multi-million dollar contracts, CBC reports.

00:01:02.423 --> 00:01:06.983
Experts warned those deals could open military data to American authorities and lock Canada

00:01:06.983 --> 00:01:08.543
deeper into foreign technology.

00:01:09.003 --> 00:01:12.923
The Department of National Defense says its systems keep government data secure inside

00:01:12.923 --> 00:01:13.423
Canada.

00:01:13.963 --> 00:01:17.783
What isn't dispute is reach independence, not whether the contracts are real.

00:01:18.895 --> 00:01:23.635
Weeks before argument, the lead plaintiff in one of two Supreme Court challenges to semi-automatic

00:01:23.635 --> 00:01:27.215
weapons bans has asked to leave the case, the New York Times reports.

00:01:27.755 --> 00:01:32.515
The paper calls that request unusual and says it scrambles a major case against Cook County.

00:01:32.895 --> 00:01:37.495
The withdrawal hits the lead name in a paired set of challenges, not a filing standing alone.

00:01:38.135 --> 00:01:40.935
Cook County's ban is what that scrambled challenge was aimed at.

00:01:41.955 --> 00:01:46.755
Houston's mayor, John Whitmeyer, has told city police to stop alerting immigration agents

00:01:46.755 --> 00:01:51.335
when a routine street stop turns up someone without legal status, the New York Times reports.

00:01:51.335 --> 00:01:56.155
The order is about those ordinary stops, not a rewrite of federal immigration law.

00:01:56.615 --> 00:01:59.175
Officers are not to make that notification in that encounter.

00:01:59.715 --> 00:02:04.095
For people without legal status on Houston streets, the change is whether local police place

00:02:04.095 --> 00:02:04.535
the call.

00:02:05.645 --> 00:02:07.585
Eddie Haymore died Wednesday at 96.

00:02:08.225 --> 00:02:13.425
Global news says a castle above Highway 97 in Peachland has marked him for decades and

00:02:13.425 --> 00:02:17.385
that he leaves ambition, controversy, and a dream that never quite landed.

00:02:17.945 --> 00:02:20.825
Locals tie his name to that castle and to Rattlesnake Island.

00:02:20.825 --> 00:02:26.005
Don Scramstad told Global News it was rattlesnake Island and a bit of trouble, a lot

00:02:26.005 --> 00:02:26.485
of trouble.

00:02:26.965 --> 00:02:32.385
A Lebanese immigrant, Hamor bought the five-acre island in 1971 to build a Middle Eastern

00:02:32.385 --> 00:02:33.545
themed amusement park.

00:02:33.885 --> 00:02:39.005
Filmmaker Greg Crompton, who made the 2019 documentary Eddie's Kingdom, said the story

00:02:39.005 --> 00:02:43.365
felt compelling as soon as ideas were being kicked around, and that he wanted to tell interesting

00:02:43.365 --> 00:02:43.925
stories.

00:02:44.365 --> 00:02:47.625
In 1974, the fight with the provincial government blew up.

00:02:47.625 --> 00:02:51.585
Haymore and his relatives took hostages at the Canadian Embassy in Beirut.

00:02:52.085 --> 00:02:56.225
Crompton said the rationale was the striking part, a mine that moved from being wronged

00:02:56.225 --> 00:02:59.965
by the government to throwing grenades into the legislature and causing mayhem.

00:03:00.365 --> 00:03:05.125
At the Peachland Museum, Assistant Curator Jeff Green said Haymore was zealously committed

00:03:05.125 --> 00:03:07.665
to the dream and chased it past every obstacle.

00:03:08.145 --> 00:03:10.285
He eventually won the legal battle with the province.

00:03:10.805 --> 00:03:12.185
The island was never developed.

00:03:12.485 --> 00:03:16.945
He built the Peachland Castle instead, and beside it a statue of himself pointing across

00:03:16.945 --> 00:03:21.985
the lake at the island. Museum worker Tracy Jains called him a visionary, impassioned,

00:03:22.305 --> 00:03:27.845
larger than life. Also today, an internal evaluation finds Northern and isolated RCMP

00:03:27.845 --> 00:03:32.685
detachments chronically and at times critically understaffed. The latest paper on retention

00:03:32.685 --> 00:03:38.685
and recruitment, CBC reports. Ottawa is preparing to widen CSSIS powers to spy abroad,

